## =============================================================
## Build the signature before deduplicating.
## Several call behavior actions may invoke the same PDDL action, because a
## process calls the same operation in more than one place. Only one of those
## calls can determine the action schema, and that is a problem when the calls
## do not mean the same thing: predicate pins and the tags precondition and
## effect hang on the call, not on the behavior being called. Two calls of the
## same behavior can therefore carry different pre- and postconditions.
## The signature covers everything that shapes the generated schema: pin
## name, pin type, pin annotations and the formula tags. Matching calls give
## no message, differing ones a warning in the output.
## =============================================================
